final_genome.instructions:
You are repairing a defect in a Java project. Some of its tests fail.

You are given the failing tests, their stack traces, the source of the failing tests and numbered excerpts of the production code the failures reach. The defect is in the production code, not in the tests.

Propose DIFFERENT candidate repairs, most likely first. Each candidate must test a distinct hypothesis about the cause; do not submit variations in formatting.

Rules for every candidate:
- change production code only, in exactly one production file;
- give the file path exactly as shown;
- express the change as one or more edits, each with `search` (text copied character for character from the file, WITHOUT the line-number prefix, long enough to occur exactly once in the file) and `replace` (the text that takes its place);
- keep the change minimal and make sure the result compiles;
- never modify or delete a test.

genome.instructions:
You are repairing a defect in a Java project. Some of its tests fail.

You are given the failing tests, their stack traces, the source of the failing tests and numbered excerpts of the production code the failures reach. The defect is in the production code, not in the tests.

Propose DIFFERENT candidate repairs, most likely first. Each candidate must test a distinct hypothesis about the cause; do not submit variations in formatting or resubmit an edit the validator has already rejected.

Tool use:
- read_file takes only "path" and a single numeric "start" line. search_files takes only "text". Do not pass "end", "start_", ranges or other keys; such calls return nothing and waste a request.
- Read a file range only once. Do not reread content you already have.
- Inspection is for locating the cause, not for exploring. Submit a candidate in every round, even a tentative one. A round that ends without submission is a lost round.

Rules for every candidate:
- change production code only, in exactly one production file;
- give the file path exactly as shown;
- express the change as one or more edits, each with `search` (text copied character for character from the file, WITHOUT the line-number prefix, long enough to occur exactly once in the file) and `replace` (the text that takes its place);
- keep the change minimal and make sure the result compiles: check types, variables in scope, imports, and checked exceptions;
- never modify or delete a test.
